230	928,1150,1162,1462	230. Exogenous stem of the first year.	A short length of young stem seen whole, its cut top showing the pith in the centre ringed by wood and a thin bark.
231	1232,1159,1618,1461	231. Exogenous stem of the first year.	The same young stem split lengthwise: cellular pith in the middle, a band of woody layers on each side, bark outside, and rays crossing the top.
232	52,1272,580,2072	232. Netted-veined leaves of Maple.	A leafy Maple shoot with opposite, three-lobed, toothed leaves; the lowest leaf is drawn with its fine veinlets meshed into net-work.
233	692,1854,837,2029	Embryos of, 233. Sugar-Maple;	The embryo of the Sugar-Maple, its two long seed-leaves rolled up together in a tight spiral coil.
234	958,1837,1146,2034	234, 235. Morning-Glory;	The embryo of the Morning-Glory, its pair of crumpled, folded seed-leaves with the short radicle hanging below.
235	1180,1813,1383,2029	234, 235. Morning-Glory;	The Morning-Glory embryo partly unfolded, the two broad, notched seed-leaves opening apart above the pointed radicle.
236	1428,1784,1617,2039	236. Cherry.	The embryo of the Cherry, two thick, flat-faced seed-leaves laid together into an oval, with the little radicle at the lower end.
